				<guid isPermaLink="false">http://filter.philitee.com/?post_type=product&#038;p=4475</guid>

					<description><![CDATA[Synthetic pocket filters are commonly used in HVAC systems because of their durability, efficiency, and versatility. Made from synthetic fibers (like polyester or polypropylene), they are designed to handle a range of environments, including humid or corrosive conditions where natural fiber filters might degrade.
<ul>
 	<li>High efficiency filtration with low resistance.</li>
 	<li>Available in wide range of size.</li>
 	<li>Gasket products available.</li>
</ul>]]></description>
										<content:encoded><![CDATA[<ul>
<li><strong>Durable Construction</strong>: Synthetic materials resist moisture and microbial growth, making them suitable for environments with high humidity or fluctuating temperatures.</li>
<li><strong>High Filtration Efficienc</strong>y: Synthetic bag filters typically have a MERV rating of 8 to 15, making them suitable for capturing fine dust, pollen, bacteria, and mold spores.</li>
<li><strong>Low Initial Pressure Drop:</strong> They allow for smooth airflow at the beginning of use, which reduces the energy demands of your HVAC system.</li>
</ul>
